cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "report-gap: calibrating model self-report against behaviour under a fixed prompt"
authors:
  - family-names: Kwon
    given-names: Alex
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-31
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/collapseindex/report-gap"
abstract: >-
  Instrumentation for measuring where a language model's self-report is a valid readout of its
  internal state. The prompt is held byte-identical across conditions and only the residual stream
  is varied, so a divergence between behavioural and verbal readouts cannot be a property of the
  stimulus. Includes a norm-matched random-direction control and a confabulation floor.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "They Infer What You Meant: Models Represent Communicative Intent More Reliably Than They Act On It"
    authors:
      - family-names: Kwon
        given-names: Alex
    year: 2026
    identifiers:
